verdict=IN-SCOPE: the approved plan's section 2 is to run the suite whole; this is the repair of what it found — a group that shipped collapsed and hid its own controls, and walks reaching for a tab strip the place hides. Self-judged.
# Self-judged. The approved plan's section 2 is "run the suite once, whole"; this
# is the repair of what that run found, which is the only reason to run it.
# 
# Four walks failed for two causes, both mine, neither a harness defect:
# 
# - The "Whole-photo tools, here only" group shipped CLOSED. A closed <details>
#   hides its contents, so aim-walk could not press #mAimDehaze at all, and
#   keep-walk and mask-fix-export-walk fell over the same way. It ships open now.
#   That is also the right product call rather than only the fix: aiming a
#   whole-photo tool at a mask is the capability 2.60 adds, and putting it behind
#   a disclosure on the release that introduces it is 040's defect — the app able
#   to do something and not saying so. The reason is recorded in the markup beside
#   the group, not only here.
# - The place takes the whole panel column, so the tab strip is not on screen
#   while it is up. A walk that enters the masks and then reaches for #ptab-export
#   waits on a control that is not there. `closeMasks()` in tools/walk-input.mjs
#   is that press, and agreement-walk, keep-walk and mask-fix-export-walk use it.
#   The walks now do what a reader does rather than reaching through the app.
# 
# Also: .control-allow loses its #colorBanner line. The sweep reaches that control
# now, so the line was a declared exception for something that no longer fails —
# and that file is checked both ways, so a stale line is itself a failure. The
# list only shrinks.
# 
# Verified individually before this commit: aim-walk, keep-walk,
# mask-fix-export-walk and agreement-walk all pass, agreement including its aimed
# arm. control-walk reads 54 against 72 on main. The place was opened and looked
# at at both widths after the change.
# 
# NOT CLAIMED: the full suite is running again as this lands and has not reported.
# Nothing is pushed to staging.
